{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You're in the ICU now. We're taking care of you for diabetic ketoacidosis. Can you tell me how you’ve been feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been really sick. Nauseous, throwing up, and this awful pain in my upper belly. It’s like my pancreas is on fire."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. Your labs show you were in DKA—diabetic ketoacidosis. That means your blood sugar was very high and your body was making ketones. We’ve started fluids and insulin to fix that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I missed some insulin. I just couldn’t keep up. But the pain—it’s not always from DKA, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're right. Your pain is likely related to your chronic pancreatitis and pancreatic issues. But right now, the DKA is the main problem. We’ll manage your pain too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. Eight weeks ago. It keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we see your history. You have pancreatic divisum and scarring, which makes you prone to this. But today, the DKA is what brought you in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Am I going to be okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re responding well. Your blood sugar is coming down, and you’re getting better. We’ll keep you in the ICU tonight, then move you to the regular floor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2159-03-23 04:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs improved overnight. Blood sugar is 292, anion gap is closing. We’re stopping the insulin drip soon and switching to shots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Shots? I was on U500 at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but we’re switching to U100 Regular insulin because it’s easier to get at pharmacies. You know how to use both, so we’ll go with what’s available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess that’s fine. But I need my pain meds. I’m hurting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re continuing your Dilaudid 6mg every 3 hours as needed. You can take it now if you’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2159-03-23 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, please. The pain is bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2159-03-23 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re transferring you to the medicine floor this afternoon. Your vitals are stable, and you’re tolerating food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2159-03-23 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But where will I go after? I don’t have a place right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2159-03-23 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re working on that. Social work found temporary housing for you. You’ll have a place to go when you’re discharged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2159-03-23 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been so stressed about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2159-03-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your blood sugar is 180 this morning—much better. We’re keeping you on the new insulin schedule. Any nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2159-03-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little, but not like before. The prochlorperazine helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2159-03-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep it as needed. Your lipase was normal, so no sign of acute pancreatitis this time—just the chronic pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2159-03-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the pain isn’t from a flare-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2159-03-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not this time. It’s likely from your chronic condition and the DKA. As your body recovers, the pain should ease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2159-03-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your A1c came back—it’s 11.6%. That means your diabetes has been poorly controlled over the last few months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2159-03-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know. I try, but sometimes I just can’t do it all."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2159-03-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re not judging. We want to help. Diabetes education will talk to you today about ways to make it easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2159-03-25 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll listen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2159-03-26 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Blood sugar is steady, and you’ve had no vomiting. We’re planning to discharge you in a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2159-03-26 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But what about my meds? I lost everything when I left my last place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2159-03-26 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a 7-day supply of all your medications when you leave. That’ll give you time to get them refilled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2159-03-26 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. And the insulin? Will I go back to U500?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2159-03-26 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can use U100 for now. If you need U500 later, your doctor can help, but U100 is what’s available in most pharmacies."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2159-03-27 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your labs are normal now. Blood sugar is 130, no ketones. You’re almost ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2159-03-27 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. But I’m scared I’ll end up back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2159-03-27 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We are too. That’s why we’re stressing follow-up. You’ll see your PCP soon, and we’ll help connect you with support."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2159-03-27 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have a guardian. She helps me make decisions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2159-03-27 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve spoken with her. She supports your care plan, so we can move forward safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. We’re finalizing your discharge. You’ve done really well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. No pain, not nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll send you home with your meds, instructions, and follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I see a specialist for my pancreas?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re scheduled to follow up with gastroenterology. They’ll manage your chronic pancreatitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mental health? I’ve been struggling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2159-03-28 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll follow up with your behavioral health provider. We know this is hard, and support is available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check before discharge. You’re alert, pain-free, and labs are stable. Ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. Thank you for helping me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember—take your insulin, manage your diet, and call if you’re not feeling well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do everything we can to help you stay healthy. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2159-03-29 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2159-03-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—your discharge papers are ready. You’ll get a ride to your new housing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2159-03-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2159-03-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve got it covered. And remember—your PCP appointment is in three days. Please go."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2159-03-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2159-03-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your urine test showed benzodiazepines, but no other drugs. Just want to make sure you’re safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2159-03-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take diazepam for anxiety. It’s prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2159-03-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s on your list. Just confirming. All good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2159-03-29 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for checking."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2159-03-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re discharging you soon. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2159-03-29 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m good. Just ready to rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2159-03-29 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve earned it. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2159-03-29 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The transport is here. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2159-03-29 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2159-03-29 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2159-03-29 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll remember that."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2159-03-23 04:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2159-03-29 14:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting, found to be due to diabetic ketoacidosis. She was transferred from the ED to the MICU for management, where she received IV fluids, insulin drip, and electrolyte repletion. The insulin drip was discontinued and transitioned to subcutaneous U100 Regular insulin due to community pharmacy availability. Her blood glucose stabilized, and she tolerated oral intake. Chronic abdominal pain was managed with her home Dilaudid regimen. Social work secured temporary housing. She received diabetes education and was discharged home with a 7-day medication supply, follow-up appointments, and instructions for ongoing care.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Chronic pancreatitis",
      "Anomalies of pancreas",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Borderline personality disorder",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Pure hypercholesterolemia",
      "Other chronic pain"
    ]
  }
}
